// Chapter 10: A wedding in the neighbourhood, in English. Translated by Claude Code from chapter10.ink; it
// follows that file line for line (same knots, lines, speakers, expressions and choice ids; the parity test in
// Story/Tests checks it). Change the dialect file first, then this one. [[word]] marks a tap-to-explain word; its
// English meaning is in the Glossary table.

EXTERNAL chose(knot)

// The callback for c2_groom, saved under chapter 2's basil_pots (see chapter10.ink).
=== wedding_lights ===
See the lights? Didn't I say he was a good one? I brought him to the café, so I married him off to Dr. Hiba! #samira #smile
{
- chose("basil_pots") == "honest":
    And you, Salma, told him the truth to his face, and I was so upset… turns out it was the best thing you ever did. #samira
- else:
    And you told him the café was open to him any time. The poor man believed you, came at night… and found the doctor! #samira
}
So you're the one who married them off, [[Khalto]]? #salma #smile
Of course! And I swear on my children, the next wedding is yours. #samira
-> END

=== street_arch ===
The flower arch went up at the café door, and Um Rami arrived with the first pot. #sys
The whole wedding order is mine: [[mansaf]] for the entire street. My first big order. #um_rami #smile
What do you need? Just say. #lana
Nothing, sweetheart. Today you're the guests. #um_rami
A flower arch, and Um Rami's mansaf… Teta would have danced. #salma #smile
-> END

=== dessert_table ===
Taste it, Uncle. And tell me the truth. No flattery. #salma
Abu Fadi took a bite and said nothing. Then he took another. #sys
That's it. The same knafeh as the summer of '74… even the cardamom in the syrup. #abu_fadi #smile
So we got it right? Finally! #lana #smile
-> END

=== family_table ===
Nawal arrived from Riyadh before sunset. #sys
Salma? Oh my… you look so much like my mother. #nawal #smile
Rana came late, after the wedding procession. She stopped at the café door, and didn't go in. #sys
You put the table outside… for me? #rana #surprised
Aunt Rana… I'm Lana. #lana
I know. Your Teta sent me your photos every Eid. #rana #sad
-> END

=== two_chairs ===
Two chairs side by side. Nawal sat down, and after a while, so did Rana. Neither of them spoke. #sys
Did your mom read the page? #lana
Twice. And she didn't say a word. #salma
So what do we do now? #lana #thinking
Nothing. Teta used to say: the first cup is for the guest, the second is for talk. #salma
-> END

// The last two lines are the season 2 teaser.
=== wedding_night ===
Yazan played, and the whole street danced the [[dabke]] under the lights, the bride and groom in the middle. #sys
Salma… I don't want to sell my half. #lana
Me neither. So… business partners? No. Sisters. #salma #smile
Sisters. And next? [[Gahwit Sitti]], the Riyadh branch. #lana #smile
Amid the joyful ululating, a letter arrived for Abu Fadi. On the envelope, a stamp from Jeddah. #sys
He knew the handwriting at first glance, and slipped it into his pocket without opening it. #sys
-> END

// Memory 10 (pour): in the present, not 1974.

=== m10_lead ===
The letter can wait. Tonight has other work. #abu_fadi
Your Teta asked for two cups. Come on, girls, bring the little dallah. #abu_fadi #smile
-> END

=== m10_intro ===
Two cups, the way Teta asked: one for me, and one for you. #salma
No. You pour for my mother, and I'll pour for yours. #lana
Like guests. The first cup is for the guest. #salma #smile
-> END

=== m10_perfect ===
Exactly like that. Patience and a steady hand… just like her. #abu_fadi #smile
-> END

=== m10_ok ===
Teta used to say: coffee forgives, like good people do. #salma #smile
-> END

=== m10_outro ===
Salma set her cup in front of Aunt Nawal, and Lana set hers in front of Aunt Rana. #sys
Twenty years, Nawal… #rana #sad
I promised her. #nawal
Rana didn't answer. She reached across the table and took her sister's hand. #sys
-> END

=== m10_return ===
Your Teta told me: they'll only ever sit together at a wedding. When they do, give them this. #abu_fadi
I put it in the drawer, girls, where the first letter was. #abu_fadi #smile
-> END

// Letter 6, to Salma and Lana.
=== letter_6 ===
To Salma and Lana, #letter
If this has reached you, your mothers have drunk coffee at one table. Thank God. #letter
In '74 I promised Abu Fadi to name the café for my children. I never wrote their names. #letter
I was waiting to see them together. Now you've seen it for me. #letter
Write under the sign: Rana and Nawal. In your own hands, not a stranger's. #letter
The little dallah is yours, both of you. Pour for each other, and don't keep count. #letter
— Your Teta #letter_signature
-> END

=== voice_6 ===
My heart, weddings bring back together what anger pulled apart. Congratulations to the couple, whoever they are. #teta
-> END

=== notify_6 ===
Got the photo: my name and my sister's under my mother's sign. Tomorrow morning, I'm coming in. #rana
-> END
